 ```
 
 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z", "due_date": null }`.
+`due_date` is a calendar date as a `YYYY-MM-DD` string, or `null` when the task has none (the default).
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
 | `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` and an optional `"due_date"` | 201, the task, or 400 for a bad `due_date` |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title`, `done` and / or `due_date` (`null` clears it; leaving it out keeps it) | 200, the task, 400 for a bad `due_date`, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
+A `due_date` that is not a real `YYYY-MM-DD` date (`2026-1-5`, `tomorrow`, `2026-02-30`, a number…) answers 400
+`{ "error": "due_date must be a date in YYYY-MM-DD format" }` and nothing is saved.
+
 Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
 
 ## Layout
 
 - `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
